+3.8.  Field Rules
+   Step 7 of Section 3.2 and step 3 of Section 3.4 apply the rules of
+   this section.  Table 4 lists every member of the predicate of a
+   decision receipt that this document admits, and Table 5 every member
+   of the predicate of an outcome receipt, each with its full path in
+   predicate, where [] stands for each entry of an array.  The rules
+   follow the strict v0.1 form of [PB-DECISION] and [PB-OUTCOME] and
+   their machine schemas, restricted to the members this document
+   admits; where Section 3.2 is stricter, the table gives the stricter
+   rule.  This section states these rules itself, and its tables follow
+   those documents as they stand at commit
+   e1fec86351b216af369a2e6ac106dcc41aaf4b4c of [PB-REPO], where the
+   machine schemas are the same as in version 6.4.0.
+   In the column Type, a digest is an object with exactly one member,
+   sha256, whose value is 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits; a timestamp
+   is an [RFC3339] UTC timestamp with a trailing "Z"; typedDigest has
+   the form given in step 7 of Section 3.2; a string is any JSON string,
+   and a non-empty string has at least one character; a boolean is one
+   of the JSON values true or false; any value is any JSON value.  The
+   type object admits only the members listed for it, and the type open
+   object admits any members.  The type names preActionAuthorization and
+   outcome allow only the JSON strings "preActionAuthorization" and
+   "outcome", respectively.  The type "0.1." and one or more digits
+   means a string consisting of "0.1." followed by one or more ASCII
+   decimal digits.  The notes (1) to (4) follow the tables.
+   Required yes means that the member MUST be present whenever the
+   object or array entry that contains it is present.  Null yes means
+   that the member may be null.  Everywhere else a null is not allowed,
+   also inside an open object and in an array of any values.  A member
+   that the table does not list for an object that is not open is not
+   allowed, at the top level of predicate as well.
