+   The proofbundle 6.4.0 commands used here receive no action bytes,
+   effect bytes, expected executor.id or consumption state, and no
+   expected decisionMaker.id.  They reject F1, F2 and F4 and return exit
+   code 0 for the other seven command-line inputs.  The procedures
+   specified here reject F3, F5, F6, F7, F8 and F9.  F10 instead passes
+   receipt verification and is refused by the relying party under
+   Section 4 with c1; its acceptance by these commands does not test
+   consumption-state enforcement.  F9 shows why checking only the
+   decision's expiry is insufficient.  At the stated T of 09:16 the
+   decision passes step 9 of Section 3.2, while the approval expired at
+   09:15.  Its validity.expiresAt exceeds the validUntil of ap, so the
+   Case 1 time-bound condition of Section 3.3 is violated independently
+   of T.
